Vulkan transfers recorded into the draw batch; NV3089 readback skipped when guest memory already holds the bytes (MAGI-5)

USER: gameplay laggy. With 0072 the main PPU thread waits on the RSX drain
(0065's RunJobChain wait) for the drain's own work, so drain time is frame
time. Three exact changes (same commands, same order, same guest bytes):

1. rsx_vulkan_backend.c: uploads (color_target_write, texture uploads,
   target seeds), clears, surface -> texture region copies, depth
   snapshots and new images' layout moves are recorded into the open draw
   batch behind the same global barrier a draw uses (vk_rec_begin /
   vk_rec_end), instead of each flushing the batch and doing its own
   submit-and-wait. Upload staging comes from a ring that lives as long as
   the batch (vk_bstage; rewound by vk_batch_reset, a full ring flushes
   first). Readbacks, presents and object destruction still flush and wait.
   The scratch depth image grows to cover both dimensions instead of being
   recreated whenever a draw alternates between 1024x1024 and 1280x720.
   PS3RECOMP_VK_BATCH=0 keeps one submit-and-wait per operation.
2. rsx_draw_engine.c: guest_read skips its readback when the rectangle lies
   inside the one guest_wrote last pushed, nothing has drawn or cleared
   into the surface since (color_serial), and the guest bytes still equal
   the copy kept then (memcmp): the readback would store the same bytes.
   Tokyo Jungle copies a main-memory buffer into its scene target and
   straight back out every frame. RSX_ENGINE_CLEAN_SKIP=0 reads back anyway.
3. The A,R,G,B <-> R,G,B,A swizzles of guest_read/guest_wrote are 32-bit
   rotates the compiler vectorises (were byte loops, ~10% of the drain
   each way).

A/B (tools/prof/drive_gameplay.py, both runs at the same time, 60 s of
Survival tutorial gameplay): mg5-bb1 22.80 flips/s vs mg5-bb0 (build/
0001-0073) 20.35, +12%; 0 FATAL, 0 LIFT-GAP both. Street frames match
(mean |diff| 0.3-0.6, wolf positions / hunger counter); the Pomeranian
close-up matches (flip 5400 vs 5468, mean |diff| 0.1 at 160x90).
check_no_emulation OK.

